WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
Web security leaves teams with two choices:

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.400
Allow everything or block everything.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.900
Both fail.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.800
People still need the web to work.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.640
They browse, search, and work every day.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.440
A simple allow-or-block choice breaks down.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.560
A normal work search starts with an ordinary web request.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.120
Binary control fails.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.640
The screen shows allow, block, and unknown.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.440
Unknown is allowed, while useful tools can be blocked.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.400
That is where the gap appears.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.320
That is where the leak can happen.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.040
Even an ordinary travel site is still a request.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.680
The request reaches the local network first.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.320
The gateway sees the traffic and records the action.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.880
The request moves through infrastructure the organization controls.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.040
Then it reaches the internet.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.800
Vendor-cloud inspection sends the log out.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.760
Trusted traffic is allowed.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.840
Unknown traffic is isolated before the session reaches the endpoint.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:03.800
The user keeps working, while the isolated session stays away from the endpoint.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.040
Amastan is more than a proxy.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:11.720
It is a self-hosted AI Secure Web Gateway, built to run in your VPC or data center.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:15.280
The decision and audit log stay on infrastructure you control.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.960
Classification can improve from traffic and feedback in that environment.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.640
Trusted traffic is allowed.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:26.040
An administrator can create a remote isolation session and test the URL requested by the user.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:31.760
The session runs remotely, keeping the web content away from the endpoint, while the user continues working.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.360
Dangerous traffic is blocked.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.320
Amastan is not your SIEM.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.800
Your SIEM collects and correlates the evidence.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.280
Amastan makes the web decision and feeds it the audit log.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.680
It is not your antivirus or EDR.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.240
Those protect the endpoint.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.920
It is not your factory firewall.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:53.760
Amastan focuses on HTTP and HTTPS content and web policy.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.600
And it is not your mail gateway.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.520
Amastan protects what happens when a user follows a link into the web.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.920
Amastan works alongside these controls,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.680
adding a dedicated layer of web security without replacing them.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.440
I am Qalbeddine.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.960
I build a system that decides what returns when people open a browser.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:17.160
If you need that control without it running in their data, Amastan is built for that.
